      "id": "clm_01M4W03X0FZNH02X0ZKYV1JBRW",
      "statement": "Zechariah 9–11 was composed by Zechariah son of Iddo after 518 BC.",
      "layer": "reconstruction",
      "passage": "Zech.9.1",
      "classification": "disputed",
      "reasoning": "Keil defends Zechariah's authorship from the post-exilic setting and tradition. Mitchell assigns 9:1–10 to 333 BC (Tyre not yet taken; 9:8 reflecting Alexander's sparing of Jerusalem), 9:11–11:3 to the reign of Ptolemy III (247–222) and 11:4–17 to another writer soon after Raphia (217); older critics (answered by Keil) proposed pre-exilic dates. No external evidence decides it.",
