    {
      "id": "clm_01M4W03X0FW8CHR8D7F6ZPSQMR",
      "statement": "Alexander's army took Damascus (333), Tyre (summer 332, after a long siege) and Gaza (332) — the cities named in Zech 9:1–7.",
      "layer": "evidence",
      "passage": null,
      "classification": "strongly_supported",
      "reasoning": "Arrian (read directly) records Parmenio's seizure of Damascus, the capture of Tyre in Hecatombaion under the archon Anicetus, and the storming of Gaza; Josephus (read directly) independently gives seven months for the siege of Tyre and two for Gaza. Whether Zech 9 refers to these events is an interpretation, recorded on the prophecy.",
